On Thu, May 14, 2009 at 10:45 AM, Ryan Leach <rsw.leach@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm sure as to the differences between the two suggestions you offered
> me. How do the meaning differ? Or do they?

"kamtsa" is a single word, a lujvo. "ka tsali kei" is a construction
that functions as a tanru unit. Their meaning is basically the same,
but they might interact differently with other words in a sentence.
The terminator "kei" can sometimes be left out, depending on what
comes after it.

